t = 50) -> Optional[dict]:\n978:恐惧贪婪指数：{fg}\n1786:def _format_hourly_score_line(symbol: str, pd: dict, ind: dict, regime: str, fg: int, fr: float, btc_ind: dict) -> str:\n1789:    score, direction = calc_score(symbol, score_pd, ind, regime, fg, fr, btc_ind)\n1837:    fg: int,\n1845:    if fg < 25:\n1846:        fg_text = \"极度恐惧\"\n1847:        fg_color = \"🔴\"","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1781007080387}}
{"type":"message","id":"f1ae1014","parentId":"36d117e2","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:11:23.177Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! `sentiment_score` is defined at line 485 but apparently it's NOT called in `calc_score`! Let me look at calc_score more carefully to see if the sentiment/fg/fr is incorporated there.\n\nLet me read the full calc_score function.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_z7jBIBjrQ39qMnULlceg8830","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":512,"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","limit":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":406,"output":202,"cacheRead":40704,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41312,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781007080409}}
{"type":"message","id":"bda3929e","parentId":"f1ae1014","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:11:23.250Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_z7jBIBjrQ39qMnULlceg8830","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    返回 (score, direction)\n    direction: 'LONG' | 'SHORT' | 'NONE'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not ind or not price_data:\n        return 0, \"NONE\"\n\n    price      = float(price_data.get(\"price\") or ind.get(\"last_close\") or 0)\n    # 成交量：优先 15m K 线 vol_current（与 vol_avg20 同量纲），避免 WS 24h 量纲不一致\n    vol        = float(ind.get(\"vol_current\") or price_data.get(\"volume\") or 0)\n    vol_avg    = ind[\"vol_avg20\"]\n    atr_pct    = ind[\"atr_pct\"]\n    resistance = ind[\"resistance\"]\n    support    = ind[\"support\"]\n\n    long_score  = 0\n    short_score = 0\n\n    # ① 价格突破（40 分）\n    if price >= resistance * 0.999:\n        long_score += 40\n    if price <= support * 1.001:\n        short_score += 40\n\n    # ② 成交量放大确认（30 分）\n    if vol > vol_avg * 1.5:\n        long_score  += 30\n        short_score += 30\n    elif vol > vol_avg * 1.2:\n        long_score  += 15\n        short_score += 15\n\n    # ③ ATR 波动率适中（20 分）\n    if 0.005 < atr_pct < 0.03:\n        long_score  += 20\n        short_score += 20\n\n    # ④ BTC 大盘方向（10 分）- 2026-03-28 老公指示：用 BTC 代替 ETH\n    _btc = btc_ind if btc_ind else {}\n    if _btc:\n        btc_bull = _btc.get(\"ema20_15m\", 0) > _btc.get(\"ema60_15m\", 0)\n        if btc_bull:\n            long_score  += 10\n            short_score -= 5\n        else:\n            short_score += 10\n            long_score  -= 5\n\n    long_score  = max(0, long_score)\n    short_score = max(0, short_score)\n\n    threshold = CONFIG[\"score_threshold\"][regime]\n    # 单币阈值加成：低胜率币种提高门槛\n    threshold += CONFIG[\"score_threshold\"].get(\"per_symbol_bonus\", {}).get(symbol, 0)\n    if long_score > short_score and long_score >= threshold:\n        return long_score, \"LONG\"\n    elif short_score > long_score and short_score >= threshold:\n        return short_score, \"SHORT\"\n\n    return max(long_score, short_score), \"NONE\"\n\n\n[2218 more lines in file. Use offset=572 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1781007083238}}
{"type":"message","id":"2e4f3cb5","parentId":"bda3929e","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:11:42.473Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! The `calc_score` function does NOT call `sentiment_score` at all! The `sentiment_score` method is defined but never invoked in the scoring pipeline. The only things that affect the score are:\n1. Price breakout (40 pts)\n2. Volume confirmation (30 pts)\n3. ATR volatility (20 pts)\n4. BTC trend (10 pts)\n\nSo my change to `sentiment_score` actually has **zero effect** on the trading decisions! The sentiment engine (`SentimentEngine`) is only used for:\n1. Caching fear & greed data (`fg_cache`)\n2. Caching funding rates (`fr_cache`)\n3. Formatting the hourly report line\n\nBut the `calc_score` function ignores `fg` and `funding_rate` parameters completely. Wait, let me check if `calc_score` even receives fg and fr...\n\nLooking at the function signature: `calc_score(symbol, price_data, ind, regime, fg, funding_rate, btc_ind)` - it receives `fg` and `funding_rate` but never uses them!\n\nThis is a major bug. The sentiment scoring was designed but never wired into the actual signal calculation! That means:\n- The system has been running purely on technical indicators (price breakout, volume, ATR, BTC trend)\n- Fear & Greed and funding rates have zero impact on trading decisions\n- The contrarian bias I identified earlier was actually NOT the cause of the problem\n\nSo the real question is: why is the system picking wrong direction if sentiment isn't even in play?\n\nGoing back to the scoring:\n1. Price breakout (40 pts) - goes with momentum direction\n2. Volume confirmation (30 pts) - neutral, both get same\n3. ATR volatility (20 pts) - neutral, both get same\n4. BTC trend (10 pts) - follows BTC direction\n\nIn a bear market:\n- BTC trend gives +10 to SHORT, -5 to LONG\n- Price breakout gives points based on whether price crosses resistance (LONG) or support (SHORT)\n- Volume and ATR are neutral\n\nSo the signal is essentially: go LONG when price breaks resistance, go SHORT when it breaks support, with a slight bias from BTC direction.\n\nThe problem might be: in a choppy bear market, the price briefly breaks above resistance (false breakout), gets a LONG signal, then reverses and drops. This is a classic false breakout problem.\n\nAnd also: the resistance/support levels depend on how they're calculated. If they're calculated from rolling windows, they might not update fast enough in a trending market.\n\nBut let me focus on the bigger issue: `sentiment_score` was never wired into `calc_score`. This means my edit to `sentiment_score` won't fix anything. I need to either:\n1. Wire `sentiment_score` into `calc_score` \n2. Or find a different fix\n\nLet me tell the user about this discovery. The scoring system itself has a design disconnect - sentiment was meant to be part of it but was never actually integrated.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"等等，发现一个更大的问题。\n\n`sentiment_score` 根本没被 `calc_score` 调用。它定义在类里但从来没有接入评分流程——`calc_score` 虽然接收了 `fg` 和 `funding_rate` 参数，但直接忽略了它们。\n\n也就是说刚才我改的那段代码**对实际交易零影响**，因为情绪加分从一开始就没生效过。\n\n真正的评分只有四项：\n1. 价格突破阻力/支撑 → 40 分\n2. 成交量放大 → 30 分（中性）\n3. ATR 适中 → 20 分（中性）\n4. BTC 大盘方向 → 10 分\n\n跟我之前说的不一样——不是情绪加分的锅，是**价格突破信号在下跌市里出假突破**：价格短暂刺破阻力位触发做多，然后掉头继续跌。\n\n真正有效的修复方向有两个：\n- **把情绪加分接进去**（原本设计就有，但没接），极端恐惧时给空头加分\n- **或者加个趋势过滤器**，BTC 下行的 EMA 线斜率超过一定阈值时禁止做多\n\n老公你看走哪个方向？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":676,"output":1516,"cacheRead":41216,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43408,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781007083258}}
{"type":"message","id":"6272db3a","parentId":"2e4f3cb5","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:15:45.638Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6db4702764a8b1d15ba954f6ac9\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"sender\": \"用户124241\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Tue 2026-06-09 20:15 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"用户124241 (ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"name\": \"用户124241\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6db4702764a8b1d15ba954f6ac9]\n用户124241: 你觉得呢"}],"timestamp":1781007345624}}
{"type":"message","id":"7e604991","parentId":"6272db3a","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:16:11.175Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for my recommendation. Let me think about which approach is better.\n\nOption 1: Wire sentiment_score into calc_score - this adds the emotion/fear dimension. In extreme fear (fg < 25), it would add bonus to shorts, and in extreme greed (fg > 75), it would add bonus to longs. This is the original design intention but needs a clear direction.\n\nOption 2: Add a trend filter - if BTC is in a clear downtrend, block longs entirely (or vice versa).\n\nI think the best approach is actually both, but the most impactful one is Option 1 - wiring sentiment into the score. Here's my reasoning:\n\n1. Sentiment was designed but never connected - fixing this alone would already help\n2. The sentiment data is already being fetched (fg_cache, fr_cache) - it's just not being used\n3. In the current market (fg=10 extreme fear), this would give LONG signals a penalty and SHORT signals a bonus, naturally biasing the system with the trend\n4. A trend filter is more of a blunt instrument and could miss reversal opportunities\n\nBut I need to think about how to wire it in. The current sentiment_score function returns just the bonus. It's called with a direction parameter. So the way to wire it would be:\n\nAfter calculating long_score and short_score (from the 4 technical factors), add:\n```python\nlong_score += sentiment_score(symbol, \"LONG\", fg, fr)\nshort_score += sentiment_score(symbol, \"SHORT\", fg, fr)\n```\n\nBut wait, `sentiment_score` is a method on `SentimentEngine`, not a standalone function. And `calc_score` is a standalone function. So I'd need to either:\n- Create the SentimentEngine instance accessible to calc_score\n- Or inline the logic\n\nLet me also reconsider the sentiment scoring. Currently:\n- LONG: fg<25 gives +10 (removed by my edit, now it's fg<40 gives +5), fr< -0.001 gives +5\n- SHORT: fg>75 gives +10, fg>60 gives +5, fr>0.002 gives +5\n\nFor our current situation (fg=10, extreme fear):\n- LONG gets: +5 (fg<40) + possible +5 from fr = max +10\n- SHORT gets: 0 from fg, possible +5 from fr. That's max +5.\n\nThis still gives more bonus to LONG in extreme fear! That doesn't help.\n\nI should flip the logic: in extreme fear, SHORT should get bonus, not LONG. Let me redesign:\n\n```python\nif direction == \"LONG\":\n    if fg < 25:       bonus -= 5    # 极度恐惧 → 扣做多分\n    elif fg > 75:     bonus += 10   # 极度贪婪 → 适合做多\n    elif fg > 60:     bonus += 5\n    if fr < -0.001:   bonus += 5    # 空头付费，多头有利\nelif direction == \"SHORT\":\n    if fg > 75:       bonus -= 5    # 极度贪婪 → 扣做空分\n    elif fg < 25:     bonus += 10   # 极度恐惧 → 适合做空\n    elif fg < 40:     bonus += 5\n    if fr > 0.002:    bonus += 5    # 多头付费过高，反转信号\n```\n\nThis way, in extreme fear (current market):\n- LONG: -5 penalty + possible +5 from fr = 0 to +5\n- SHORT: +10 bonus + possible +5 from fr = +10 to +15\n\nThis would significantly bias toward shorts in extreme fear markets, which is what we want.\n\nBut the user hasn't asked me to redesign the sentiment scoring - they asked which direction to go. Let me give my recommendation.\n\nI think the right approach is to wire sentiment into calc_score AND fix the sentiment logic to actually be useful:\n\n1. Wire the sentiment_score into calc_score (it was designed for this but never connected)\n2. The sentiment logic should actually be contrarian-correct: fear → favor shorts, greed → favor longs\n\nThis is both the right thing to do (it completes the original design) and has the most impact (sentiment directly influences direction).\n\nLet me recommend this to the user concisely.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"两个都做，但优先把情绪加分接进去。理由：\n\n**情绪原本就是评分的一部分**，代码都写好了只是忘了接——fg 和 fr 传进了 `calc_score` 但函数里完全没用。接上之后极端恐惧天然利空多头、利多空头，等于趋势过滤器也顺便有了。\n\n具体就是改两处：\n1. `calc_score` 里把 `sentiment_score` 接进去，给 long/ short 各加上对应情绪分\n2. 情绪逻辑反过来：恐惧时利好做空而不是做多——现在的逻辑是「别人恐慌我贪婪」，但事实证明这招在单边市里不管用\n\n接上后当前极端恐惧的市场（fg=10），空头会有 +10 以上的情绪加成，多头的分数会被压下去，自然就不会乱接飞刀了。\n\n要改吗？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1197,"output":2065,"cacheRead":41856,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45118,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781007345636}}
