{"type":"message","id":"92ff1781","parentId":"4e3e2f90","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:17:34.285Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to:\n1. Modify the sentiment_score logic (already partially done, but need to reverse the logic)\n2. Wire sentiment_score into calc_score\n3. Update related files: SOUL.md, strategy docs, etc.\n\nLet me think through the changes:\n\n**1. `sentiment_score` logic reversal:**\nInstead of \"fear → go long\" and \"greed → go short\", it should be \"fear → go short\" and \"greed → go long\":\n- fg < 25 (extreme fear): bonus for SHORT (+10), not LONG\n- fg < 40 (fear): bonus for SHORT (+5)\n- fg > 75 (extreme greed): bonus for LONG (+10)\n- fg > 60 (greed): bonus for LONG (+5)\n- fr < -0.001 (shorts paying longs): bonus for SHORT (shorts are crowded, contrarian)\n- fr > 0.002 (longs paying shorts): bonus for LONG\n\nWait, actually let me reconsider. The funding rate logic... if funding rate is negative (shorts pay longs), that means there are more shorts than longs. In a bearish market, this makes sense - everyone's shorting. The contrarian play would be to go long. But in a sustained bear market, that's not good.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The user's problem is \"一直找不对方向\" - the system keeps picking wrong direction. The original sentiment logic was \"fear → go long\" (buy when others are fearful), which is the Warren Buffett approach. But in practice, especially in crypto where trends can last long, this contrarian approach leads to catching falling knives.\n\nThe fix should be:\n- Fear → bonus for SHORT (trend following in fear)\n- Greed → bonus for LONG (trend following in greed)\n- Funding rate: fr < -0.001 (shorts paying) → bonus for SHORT (follow the crowd since they're right about the trend)\n- Funding rate: fr > 0.002 (longs paying too much) → bonus for LONG\n\nActually wait, if funding rate is negative (shorts paying), that means there are many short positions. This could mean:\na) The crowd is right and price keeps dropping (momentum) → go SHORT\nb) The crowd is too crowded and will get squeezed → go LONG\n\nSince the user's problem is false LONG signals in a bear market, I should go with (a) - follow the momentum.\n\n**2. Wire into `calc_score`:**\nAdd the sentiment bonus to long_score and short_score before the threshold check.\n\n**3. Files to update:**\n- `crypto_signal_monitor.py` - main code change\n- `SOUL.md` - update scoring logic description\n- `AGENTS.md` - update strategy description if needed\n\nLet me also check if there's a separate strategy configuration file.\n\nLet me start making changes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"好，先确认所有要动的文件，然后一次性改完。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_OZYGPogIUsf1Rr7Iu0EG8365","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -rn '情绪\\|sentiment\\|恐惧贪婪\\|fg.*score\\|calc_score\\|评分' /root/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md /root/.openclaw/workspace/AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":524,"output":1381,"cacheRead":43008,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":44913,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781007438403}}
