{"type":"message","id":"26e58489","parentId":"58b99f6c","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:20:18.838Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, there's a logic inconsistency in the comments of the LONG direction:\n- `fr > 0.002 → bonus += 5 # 多头付费过高，做多拥挤 → 反转做空，此处不适用`\n\nThis says \"longs paying too much → crowded longs → reversal to SHORT, not applicable here\"? But we're giving +5 bonus to LONG. That's wrong!\n\nLet me think about this:\n- `fr > 0.002` means longs are paying shorts (funding rate is positive and high)\n- This means there are more longs than shorts (longs are paying shorts to keep their positions)\n- In a contrarian sense, this means longs are overcrowded → potential reversal → should go SHORT\n- But we're giving bonus to LONG? That's inconsistent!\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read my own comment: \"多头付费过高，做多拥挤 → 反转做空，此处不适用\". This says the funding rate bonus for LONG is wrong. The comment literally says \"不适用\" (not applicable). So I should either:\n1. Remove the bonus (since it contradicts the sentiment logic)\n2. Or change this line to give bonus to SHORT instead\n\nLet me think about this properly. The user's problem was \"fear → going long catches falling knives.\" The fix is trend-following: fear → short, greed → long.\n\nFor funding rates:\n- fr > 0.002: longs paying shorts (very positive). More longs than shorts. In a bull market, this is normal. In a reversal, longs get squeezed. The contrarian play is SHORT.\n- fr < -0.001: shorts paying longs (very negative). More shorts than longs. In a bear market, this is normal. In a reversal, shorts get squeezed. The contrarian play is LONG.\n\nSince we're now doing trend-following (not contrarian), the funding rate logic should also follow the trend:\n- fr > 0.002: longs are dominant → trend is up → bonus to LONG\n- fr < -0.001: shorts are dominant → trend is down → bonus to SHORT\n\nThis actually makes the most sense! High positive funding = lots of longs = bullish = go long. High negative funding = lots of shorts = bearish = go short.\n\nLet me fix the comments and keep the correct logic.\n\nActually, wait - the comments already say \"不适用\" but the code still adds the bonus. The behavior is correct (fr > 0.002 → long bonus, fr < -0.001 → short bonus) but the comments are confusing. Let me fix the comments.\n\nHmm, actually re-reading: \"空头付费过高，做空拥挤 → 反转做多，此处不适用\" - this says \"shorts paying too much → short crowded → reversal to long, not applicable here.\" But we're giving +5 to SHORT, which is contrarian (follow the shorts). Wait no...\n\nfr < -0.001 means FUNDING RATE is negative, which means SHORTS are paying LONGS. So shorts are the dominant side. If we follow the trend: shorts are dominant → go short → bonus to SHORT. This is correct!\n\nLet me fix the comments to be clear.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"等等，COMMENT 里的逻辑说反了。`fr > 0.002` 是多头主导（多头付钱），趋势跟随应该给多头加分，但注释写着\"不适用\"——实际上应该反过来：费率也是顺势信号。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_KyC8Ft7zJEJSFsV6W3b86601","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","new_string":"        if direction == \"LONG\":\n            if fg > 75:       bonus += 10   # 极度贪婪做多（顺势）\n            elif fg > 60:     bonus += 5\n            if fr > 0.002:    bonus += 5    # 多头付费（多头主导）→ 做多顺势\n        elif direction == \"SHORT\":\n            if fg < 25:       bonus += 10   # 极度恐惧做空（顺势，不接飞刀）\n            elif fg < 40:     bonus += 5\n            if fr < -0.001:   bonus += 5    # 空头付费（空头主导）→ 做空顺势","old_string":"        if direction == \"LONG\":\n            if fg > 75:       bonus += 10   # 极度贪婪做多（顺势）\n            elif fg > 60:     bonus += 5\n            if fr > 0.002:    bonus += 5    # 多头付费过高，做多拥挤 → 反转做空，此处不适用\n        elif direction == \"SHORT\":\n            if fg < 25:       bonus += 10   # 极度恐惧做空（顺势，不接飞刀）\n            elif fg < 40:     bonus += 5\n            if fr < -0.001:   bonus += 5    # 空头付费过高，做空拥挤 → 反转做多，此处不适用"}}