{"type":"message","id":"c57d3fbc","parentId":"3e212c7a","timestamp":"2026-06-09T13:02:37.747Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All checks passed. But wait, I notice something interesting about test #6:\n\n- Without sentiment: score=30, dir=NONE\n- With sentiment (fg=10): score=45, dir=NONE\n\nThe score went from 30 to 45 because SHORT got +15 from sentiment. But the direction is still NONE because the threshold for ranging is 30 and the score 45 is above threshold but... let me check:\n\nWait, in test #6:\n- Price = 62000, Resistance = 63000, Support = 61000\n- Price (62000) is between support and resistance, so no breakout bonus for either\n- vol_current = 50, vol_avg20 = 100, ratio = 0.5 → no volume bonus\n- ATR 0.02 → within 0.005-0.03 → both get +20\n- BTC: ema20 (61000) < ema60 (62000) → bearish → short +10, long -5\n- So: long = 20 - 0 = min 0 with clamp → 0? No wait, long: 0 (breakout) + 0 (volume) + 20 (ATR) - 5 (BTC bearish) = 15, clamped at max(0, 15) = 15\n- short: 0 (breakout) + 0 (volume) + 20 (ATR) + 10 (BTC bearish) = 30\n- threshold = 30 (ranging)\n- short_score (30) > long_score (15) but 30 ≥ 30 → should return SHORT!\n\nBut my test shows NONE, not SHORT. Hmm, that might be because I used `threshold` from `ranging` which is 30. The condition is `short_score > long_score and short_score >= threshold`. 30 > 15 and 30 >= 30 → TRUE → should be SHORT.\n\nWait, but the test output says score=45 and dir=NONE for test #6. This is because...\nActually looking again at the calc_score code:\n\n```python\nthreshold = CONFIG[\"score_threshold\"][regime]\n# 单币阈值加成\nthreshold += CONFIG[\"score_threshold\"].get(\"per_symbol_bonus\", {}).get(symbol, 0)\n```\n\n\"ranging\" threshold is 30. BTC doesn't have a per_symbol_bonus? Let me check.\n\nActually wait, the per_symbol_bonus might add extra. But regardless, with the basic check:\n- Without sentiment: short=30, long=15. short >= threshold(30) and short > long → SHORT. But the output says \"score=30, dir=NONE\". \n\nHmm, that's weird. Let me think... maybe there's something wrong with my test parameters? Actually, looking at condition more carefully:\n\n```python\nif long_score > short_score and long_score >= threshold:\n    return long_score, \"LONG\"\nelif short_score > long_score and short_score >= threshold:\n    return short_score, \"SHORT\"\nreturn max(long_score, short_score), \"NONE\"\n```\n\nFor test without sentiment: long=15, short=30, threshold=30. short_score(30) > long_score(15) and short_score(30) >= threshold(30) → True and True → SHORT.\n\nBut the output says NONE. Something's off. Let me look at the configuration more carefully. Maybe the per_symbol_bonus adds to threshold.\n\nLet me check:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_qsEBAcJ1KkAXe1NIEw9j3507","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\n# Check the CONFIG thresholds and per_symbol_bonus\nexec(open('crypto_signal_monitor.py').read().split('def calc_score')[0])\n# Actually this won't work cleanly. Let me just check the config file.\n\" 2>&1 || true\ngrep -A5 'score_threshold' /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":121,"output":1679,"cacheRead":59520,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":61320,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781010140832}}
