{"type":"message","id":"8b73ec25","parentId":"81f08bdd","timestamp":"2026-06-09T16:34:36.304Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The import of crypto_signal_monitor is taking too long (it tries to execute the whole module). Let me just check the ATR values from the indicators that the monitor calculates. I can look at the monitor log or run a simpler check.\n\nActually, let me just answer based on what I already know from the code and the position data. The TP is at 4% for all positions, which means ATR is currently below the threshold that would trigger dynamic expansion. The formula is:\n\n```python\ntp_pct = max(TAKE_PROFIT_PCT, min(atr_pct * 2.0, TP_MAX_PCT))\n```\n\nWhere TAKE_PROFIT_PCT = 4%, TP_MAX_PCT = 15%.\n\nThe dynamic range (4-15%) is: TP = max(4%, min(ATR% × 2, 15%))\n\nFor TP to go above 4%, ATR needs to be > 2%:\n- ATR = 2% → TP = 4% (still at minimum)\n- ATR = 3% → TP = 6%\n- ATR = 5% → TP = 10%\n- ATR = 7.5% → TP = 15% (capped)\n\nThe current market is likely at low-moderate ATR, hence all TPs at 4%.\n\nLet me just quickly verify with the logs what ATR values are being calculated.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_PRvyBu2Db45MO6B5Xyvy5290","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -E 'ATR|atr_pct|止盈.*动态' /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log 2>/dev/null | tail -5","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":133,"output":702,"cacheRead":78080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":78915,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781022867850}}
